It makes sense the webhook id would be persisted but I'm confused why we would persist the cloudhook url. The code below shows the cloudhook url is persisted. This example is consistent with toon and netatmo. Shouldn't the webhook id be persisted by the cloudhook url and/or webhook url be regenerated on startup?

https://github.com/home-assistant/core/blob/dev/homeassistant/components/toon/coordinator.py#L55-L72
```python
        if CONF_WEBHOOK_ID not in self.entry.data:
            data = {**self.entry.data, CONF_WEBHOOK_ID: secrets.token_hex()}
            self.hass.config_entries.async_update_entry(self.entry, data=data)

        if self.hass.components.cloud.async_active_subscription():

            if CONF_CLOUDHOOK_URL not in self.entry.data:
                webhook_url = await self.hass.components.cloud.async_create_cloudhook(
                    self.entry.data[CONF_WEBHOOK_ID]
                )
                data = {**self.entry.data, CONF_CLOUDHOOK_URL: webhook_url}
                self.hass.config_entries.async_update_entry(self.entry, data=data)
            else:
                webhook_url = self.entry.data[CONF_CLOUDHOOK_URL]
        else:
            webhook_url = self.hass.components.webhook.async_generate_url(
                self.entry.data[CONF_WEBHOOK_ID]
            )
